# Game Development

**Intent:** Build any game genre (action, puzzle, idle, narrative) with optional determinism, embeds, and PWA — not general marketing site routing (see `website-building.mdc`). UI policy on all surfaces → `universal-product.mdc` §2a.

**Tag legend:** **[core]** every game should consider; **[applicable if …]** skip when irrelevant (e.g. do not force netcode rules on a casual puzzle).

## §1 Product locks before scale **[core]**

- Lock **visual direction**, **monetization ethics** (e.g. cosmetics-only, no pay-to-win), and **renderer/runtime** early. Name the **nearest genre reference** for UI/HUD (e.g. 2048 for tile puzzles, classic brawlers for fighters) — see `universal-product.mdc` §2d.
- Record **ADRs** in `docs/decisions/` so future agents know *why*, not only *what*.
- **`[applicable if public roster / real-world names]`** — legal/name checklist before scaling content (trademark, slurs, restricted names).
- **`[applicable if freemium]`** — document DLC scope; never sell gameplay power.

## §2 Architecture: engine vs shell **[core]**

- **Pure game core** — no UI framework, no DOM, no `window` in simulation code (`packages/<engine>/` or equivalent).
- **Presentation shell** — menu routes in your web framework; Canvas/WebGL/DOM renderer **reads** core state only.
- **Versioned schemas** for entities, levels, and events so saves and replays survive refactors.

**`[applicable if action / fighting / sports / deterministic replay]`**

- **Fixed timestep** sim (e.g. 60 Hz) in core; render may interpolate.
- **Deterministic math** — fixed-point or integer-only physics; avoid raw floats for authoritative state.
- **Seeded PRNG** — all gameplay randomness from a seed stored with the replay.
- **Input ring buffer** — early presses still register within a small window.
- **Central feel module** — hitstop, shake, freeze frames in one place for designers and replay parity.
- **Replay = inputs + seed**; automated verify must reproduce identical outcomes before claiming netcode-ready.

**`[applicable if puzzle / turn-based / low stakes]`**

- Determinism optional; still separate **solver/level data** from UI; document algorithms honestly for educational hosts.

## §3 Renderer & assets **[core]**

- Pick renderer for **lowest common device** (Canvas 2D, DOM, SVG) unless you need WebGL **`[applicable if 3D or heavy particles]`**.
- Document renderer choice in an ADR (Canvas for broad mobile support vs WebGL for effects — project decides).
- **`[applicable if zero-download audio]`** — WebAudio synth / procedural SFX.
- **`[applicable if large asset pipeline]`** — lazy load, cache strategy, mobile size budget.
- **`[applicable if action / many spawned entities]`** — object pooling for bullets/particles; target ~**16 ms** sim slice per frame on low-end mobile.

## §4 Screens, embeds, and host sites **[core]**

Standalone PWA **or** iframe on a parent site:

- Detect embed: `window.self !== window.top` → compact layout class on `<html>` (project-defined prefix).
- **Iframe / shell height** — `clamp()` / `dvh` floors so menus and CTAs are not clipped; `@media (max-height: …)` fallback.
- **Touch** — minimum targets; on-screen controls when keyboard unavailable **`[applicable if mobile browser]`**.
- **`[applicable if portrait-first mobile]`** — dedicated HUD pass (after core loop is fun on landscape/desktop).
- **Host vendoring** — build with correct `base` subpath → copy to `public/games/<id>/` → host SPA fallback → theme overlay CSS for parent contrast.
- **`[applicable if educational host]`** — short note naming real algorithms used (accurate labels only).

Host routing details → `website-building.mdc` (vendored folder only).

## §5 Player experience baseline **[core]**

- Remappable controls + persisted settings **`[applicable if keyboard/gamepad]`**.
- Pause that **stops the simulation tick**, not only hides UI.
- Live audio sliders (master / SFX / music).
- In-match reference UI (moves, objectives) for onboarding.
- Local settings + progress in `localStorage` / IndexedDB **`[applicable if client-only]`**.

**Game HUD / UI:** apply `universal-product.mdc` §1b; keep HUD minimal in embeds so play area is not shrunk by ornamental chrome.

## §6 Tools & live ops (client-only) **`[applicable if designer-heavy]`**

- Local telemetry (usage, win rates) — on-device, privacy-first.
- Tuning overlay writing to local storage without redeploy for every tweak.
- Hidden admin or `noindex` QA routes; keep player navigation clean.

## §7 Delivery & hardening **[core]**

- **`[applicable if offline / installable]`** — PWA with documented SW strategy; on embed subpaths, scope or disable SW so the **parent site's** service worker and routing are not hijacked — test both standalone and iframe before ship.
- No debug globals exposing solver, full state, or level data in production; build verify fails if reintroduced.
- Minify shipped client JS; `drop_console` where appropriate; README states client bundles are not secret — license + server validation when cheating matters.
- Test on throttled network once before release.

## §8 Testing & definition of done **[core]**

- E2E (Playwright or equivalent): reach first interactive frame, complete minimal play path, screenshot on critical views.
- **`[applicable if deterministic core]`** — automated replay verification in CI.
- Smoke narrow + wide viewport; test embed and standalone if both ship.
- **`[applicable if level-based puzzle]`** — **one unit test per level** (structure + solvability where provable); shared `level-count.test.mjs` asserting N levels in source; update E2E copy when total level count changes (e.g. `Puzzle 1 / 15`, not stale `/ 3`).
- **`[applicable if embed iframe on educational host]`** — run E2E against local preview server serving `dist/client` at `/games/<slug>/`; keep `?e2e=1` auto-win paths **fast and deterministic** (instant win when puzzle already solved — do not depend on multi-second animations in CI).

## §12 Embed puzzle suite — production learnings (Bharat Brawlers / dsapatterns) **[applicable if iframe embed on parent SPA]**

Reference implementation: five TanStack Router games vendored to `public/games/<slug>/` on dsapatterns-website. Capture these before shipping the next embed game.

### Theme switcher (Equalize tokens + Tailwind)

- Import `equalize-theme-templates.css` **before** Tailwind; Tailwind `@layer base { body { background-color: var(--color-background) } }` **overrides** `body { background: var(--bg) }` — themes appear broken (always white/light).
- **Fix:** after Tailwind base, force embed shells:
  ```css
  html[class$="-embed"],
  html[class$="-embed"] body {
    background-color: var(--bg) !important;
    color: var(--txt-hi) !important;
  }
  ```
- **`useGameTheme`:** always `document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', theme)` — do not remove the attribute for midnight.
- Game shells and canvas wrappers: **`var(--bg)` / `var(--txt-hi)`**, not hardcoded `#0A0A0F`, `bg-black`, etc. Theme button needs `pointer-events: auto` and high z-index in iframe.

### Iframe height — critical UI above the fold

- Parent iframes are often **~370–500px tall** while a naive `min-h-screen` layout is **700px+**. Trays, CTAs, and instructions below the canvas are **invisible without scroll** (users report “missing mirrors / can’t play”).
- **Fix:** `h-[100dvh] flex flex-col overflow-hidden` on root; **compact header (shrink-0)** → **interactive tray / primary actions (shrink-0, above canvas)** → **playfield (`flex-1 min-h-0`)**.
- Screenshot or Playwright at **embed height**, not only full desktop viewport.

### Touch vs drag (mirror / token trays)

- HTML5 **drag-and-drop does not work reliably on mobile**. If gameplay is “drag from tray,” add **tap-to-select → tap grid cell to place** as the primary mobile path; keep drag as desktop enhancement.
- Label empty tray honestly: puzzle may need **zero tray mirrors** (beam already hits target) — say so in UI, not only in README.

### Level design at scale (15+ levels)

- **Minimum bar:** 15 levels per puzzle game in the suite; each level named and listed in source.
- **Solvability:** for ray/path puzzles, ship a **solver** (brute-force tray placement + `traceBeam`) and run in CI (`scripts/games/validate-*-puzzles.ts` or test helper). Hand-authored mirror paths must be traced — `/` vs `\` reflection is easy to get wrong.
- **Seeded procedural levels** (e.g. wire grid): `generatePuzzleForLevel(n)` with `LEVEL_COUNT = 15`; clamp level index; verify connected/solvable path for e2e `skipShuffle` builds.
- **Echo / timing games:** e2e uses `?e2e=1` to auto-complete or skip shuffle; keep **3 fast E2E specs** for levels 1–3 even when product has 15 levels.

### Game-specific pitfalls (verified in production)

| Game | Pitfall | Fix |
|------|---------|-----|
| **Laser / mirror** | Tray below fold; puzzle 1 has 0 mirrors | Tray above canvas; tap-to-place; hint when tray empty |
| **Pixel path** | Player orb only drawn when `running` | Draw orb + gold on title preview and whenever `screen === playing` |
| **Track / urgency** | Random rotation of **path** tiles → instant derail | Scramble **decoys only** when enterable but unsolved; e2e `skipShuffle` + instant win if `isPathConnected` |
| **Echo node** | Doors require plates held while walking to exit | **Latch** doors once both plates pressed together |
| **Neon circuit** | E2E expects win overlay | Pre-solved grid when `?e2e=1`; skip rotation randomization |

### Embed build pipeline (CSR in iframe)

- **`DSAPATTERNS_EMBED=1`:** Vite `ssr: false`; build → `scripts/games/patch-embed-client.mjs` (basepath) → `generate-csr-index.mjs` (single `index.html` shell) → vendor to `public/games/<slug>/`.
- Preview all five: `node scripts/games/embed-preview-server.mjs` on port 5299; Playwright `baseURL` points there.
- After deploy: purge CDN cache for `/` and `/games/*` if shell references stale JS hashes.

### Verification checklist before push

```bash
node --test tests/games/*.test.mjs          # level count + solvability
npm run build:embed:games                   # all dists + vendor
npx playwright test -c playwright.games.config.mjs
```

Do **not** commit scratch scripts (`check_*.mjs`, `staged_diff.txt`) — add to `.gitignore` if they recur.


